## Review section: Independent review & behavior-preserving refactor

> **Triggered by:** all implementation sections green.
> **Goal:** one review-and-refactor pass over the whole change (see `references/implementation-review.md`). Gates the implement gate.

- [ ] Launch a **fresh auditor subagent** (separate context, not the implementer). It loads the idiom pack(s) for every language in scope and flags unsafe/panic-prone code, idiom violations, oversized/monolithic modules, and hygiene issues.
- [ ] Record auditor findings: `review-log.mjs record --id {{id}} --stage implement --role auditor --reviewer "<label>" --verdict <approved|changes-requested> --finding "<file:line> [category] <action>"`
- [ ] Apply behavior-preserving cleanup for the findings (or record a substantive no-change rationale). Firm-seam tests stay green; a firm-seam failure is a kickback, not a test edit.
- [ ] Run the full test suite — must be green after refactor.
- [ ] Launch a **distinct fresh verifier subagent** (not the implementer or auditor). It confirms findings resolved and behavior preserved: `review-log.mjs record --id {{id}} --stage implement --role verifier --reviewer "<distinct label>" --verdict approved`
- [ ] User approves → implement gate → approved (blocked until the verifier approval is recorded)

